      "cooked": "<p>Before prattling on endlessly about my rules issue, let me say that SotM has always been a great game, but Vegeance pushed it over the top!</p><p>Anyway, enough sucking up....</p><p><span>I just recently got my copy of Vengeance, and we played a 4 player game against four of the the Five; Baron Blade, Proletariat, Friction, &amp; Ermine vs Mister Fixer, Naturalist, Parse, &amp; Dark Watch Setback.</span></p><p><span>It eventually came down to where there were only 1 villain and 1 hero remaining. Ermine vs my Dark Watch Setback.&nbsp;</span></p><p>Before stating my question, I wish to say and I searched the rulebook/official clarifications/general web for a ruling and could not find one, so if I missed it somewhere I apologize and will chastise myself severely to atone.</p><p>My question is this, in the 1v1 show down of my Setback vs Ermine, how am I supposed to handle her \"Second Lowest HP\"/\"Second Highest HP\" targeting if I am the only non-incapacitated character remaining?</p><p>During the end of the game, we played that I was not targeted, since I was consistently the highest/lowest, and avoided the damage and was able to squeak out a victory. But I cannot help but wonder if I cheated severely and have to remove the warm glowing feeling in my heart that the victory brought me.</p><p>Any ideas?</p>",
