      "id": 95219,
      "name": "Ameena",
      "username": "Ameena",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ameena/{size}/1907_2.png",
      "created_at": "2014-03-09T11:52:39.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>I'm sure this came up relatively recently (within the past couple of months or so), since I recall a discussion on the forum somewhere, the conclusion of which was that bascially you did it right - you can be the highest and the lowest at the same time, but not the <span class=\"bbcode-i\">second</span>-highest/lowest if there are no other applicable targets. So Ermine wouldn't've been able to hit you because there'd've needed to be at least one other hero target present (assuming the attack was only targeting hero targets) for one of those to be the second-lowest.</p>",
      "post_number": 4,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:21:59.626Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
